js can start a task now and finish it later without stopping the whole program 

In "JavaScript", "asynchronous" (async) behavior means:

JavaScript can start a task, move on to other work, and handle the result later when the task finishes.

Without "async" behavior, the browser would freeze every time it waited for something slow like:

API calls
Database requests
File reading
Timers
Loading images/videos

lets understand synchronus method 
js normally works with line by line 
console.log("1")
console.log("2")
console.log("3")
output will be 
1
2
3
this is called "asynchronous"execution
each line waits for previous work to finish 

             Real Difference
"Synchronous"	         "Asynchronous"
Blocks execution	      Non-blocking
Waits for task	          Continues execution
Slower UX	              Faster UX
Sequential	              Background processing
Can freeze app	          Keeps app responsive